; bin is a symlink to _build/install/default/bin, where dune installs
; the executables (their public_name) and mini-pi (below): ./bin/mini-mk.
; Dune must not follow it: it points into _build, and is dead before
; the first build.
(dirs :standard \ docs bin)

; js_of_ocaml's integer-overflow warning off: in JavaScript an int has
; 32 bits, and the code it would compile is written for that (Bits: its
; masks and unsigned comparisons; plan_web.md). What it warns about is
; such a word (0xffffffff, an instruction's encoding, whose 32 bits are
; the same as a negative int), or Pi4's and arm64's code, linked in
; MiniQemuWeb but never run by the Pi 1 board there. It gives no
; place, and misses the bug 32-bit ints did cause (TinyMachineCPU's
; unsigned comparisons by <): the checks are the runs under node.
(env
 (_
  (js_of_ocaml
   (flags (:standard -w no-integer-overflow)))))

; the script that boots the Pi kernels under mini-qemu, installed with
; the programs (dune install)
(install
 (section bin)
 (package ix)
 (files mini-pi))
